# What a fresh clone generates when it is built, tested or documented with the
# commands this repository provides. Anything an editor, a personal script or a
# one-off command leaves behind is deliberately not listed: those belong in a
# global ignore file, not here.

# CMake build trees, one per compiler/mode/consumer combination and named after
# the preset that created it. Out-of-source by design: moving off test/Makefile
# is what stopped obj_*/bin_* being generated inside the source tree. Everything
# a build produces lands in here: objects, binaries, .gcda/.gcno, CTest's
# Testing/ directory, compile_commands.json, and the top-level Makefile's
# libiov2.so (build/make/).
/build/

# The lcov summary the coverage instructions in test/README.md write, which they
# name without a path and so leave next to the sources.
coverage.info

# Doxygen output. Doxyfile.en and Doxyfile.zh both set OUTPUT_DIRECTORY = docs,
# so running either from a clone fills these two in beside the checked-in
# docs/index.html.
docs/en/
docs/zh/
